ition:** INDEPENDENT\n**Automated operational score:** 95/100 — LOW — APPROVE\n*This tool is for demonstration purposes only.*\n\n### Summary\nThe AI reviewer reported 1 confirmed actionable finding(s).\n\n### Findings\n- **LOW · SECURITY_VULNERABILITY · Admin password variable has no validation constraints and no confirmed secret-store integration**\n  - Category rationale: The variable `admin_password` accepts a caller-supplied string with no validation block enforcing minimum length, character complexity, or any constraint. The `sensitive = true` flag suppresses output redaction but does not prevent a weak or empty password from being passed. No Key Vault reference, secret data source, or external secret-store integration is present anywhere in the supplied configuration. The value will be stored in Terraform state in encrypted form only if the state backend enforces encryption; the provider.tf supplies no backend configuration, so state encryption is unconfirmed. Together these represent a concrete, low-severity weakness: a password credential with no enforced strength policy and no confirmed secret-store path.\n  - Evidence: terraform/tc15_variables.tf: `variable \"admin_password\" { description = \"Administrator password for the research database.\" type = string sensitive = true }` — no `validation` block present. No `azurerm_key_vault` or secret data source appears in any of the supplied context files (main.tf, network.tf, nsg.tf, provider.tf, outputs.tf, variables.tf).\n  - Analysis: terraform/tc15_variables.tf declares `variable \"admin_password\"` with `type = string` and `sensitive = true` but includes no `validation` block. Any caller can supply an empty string or trivially weak password. Additionally, none of the supplied Terraform files reference an `azurerm_key_vault`, `azurerm_key_vault_secret`, or equivalent data source; the password is expected to be supplied as a raw Terraform input variable rather than retrieved from a managed secret store. The `sensitive = true` attribute only redacts the value from Terraform plan/apply output; it does not enforce secrecy or strength at the infrastructure layer.\n  - Impact: A caller could supply a weak or empty password. If state is stored without backend-enforced encryption (no backend block is configured), the plaintext password value would be readable in Terraform state. For a research fixture this is low severity, but the pattern is unsafe if the variable is reused or promoted.\n  - Recommendation: Add a `validation` block enforcing a minimum length and character-class requirement. Integrate with Azure Key Vault: retrieve the secret via an `azurerm_key_vault_secret` data source and pass the secret ID rather than the raw password as an input variable. Confirm that the Terraform state backend enforces encryption at rest.\n\n### Recommendation\nReview and remediate the confirmed findings above.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6147795154/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":15368,"client_id":"Iv1.05c79e9ad1f6bdfa","slug":"github-actions","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTUzNjg=","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github","html_url":"https://github.com/github","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/repos","events_url":"